<%# locals: (icon:, icon_type: :solid, icon_class: nil) %>
<%# An icon beside a block of content -- a title and one or more paragraphs,
    sometimes a button. The sibling of ui_icon_item, which is for a single
    line: this one keeps the icon on the first line of a block that can be any
    height, so the icon sits in its own shrink-0 column rather than being a
    flex item that stretches.

    Rendered with `render layout:` because the content column is free-form.
    Nothing here assumes a title element: two callers lead with a <p> and one
    with an <h4>, and folding that in would need a knob per caller.

    gap-3, which is what two of the three callers already wrote. The block is
    taller than ui_icon_item's one line and reads better with the extra 4px. %>
<div class="flex items-start gap-3">
  <div class="shrink-0 mt-0.5">
    <%= fa_icon icon, icon_type, class: icon_class %>
  </div>
  <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
    <%= yield %>
  </div>
</div>
